j. Any other information that may be relevant.
(B) Minimum information to the Shareholders for approval of Related Party Transactions:
The notice being sent to the shareholders seeking approval for any proposed RPT shall, in addition
to the requirements under the Companies Act, 2013, include the following information as a part
of the explanatory statement:
a. A summary of the information provided by the management of the listed entity to the
audit committee as specified in paragraph 4 of this Section;
b. Justification for why the proposed transaction is in the interest of the listed entity;
c. Where the transaction relates to any loans, inter-corporate deposits, advances or
investments made or given by the listed entity or its subsidiary, the details specified
under para 4(f) above;
d. A statement that the valuation or other external report, if any, relied upon by the listed entity
in relation to the proposed transaction will be made available through the registered
